Z||000008||Oreif||03-16-2001||01:18 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stimpy:<BR><B>Check your calender, but I think May 19 is a Friday, putting FCO's show on the 20th.  But thanks for the plug!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I checked my Official Pennock's 2001 Fiero Calendar  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> (Thanks Again 85ECO!!!!) and the 19th is a Saturday. <P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Tina||03-17-2001||08:30 AM||||O.K, rather than calling some of these<BR>people and asking all the dumb Questions.<BR>Perhaps, you guys and girls can fill in the blanks.<BR> <BR>Been to car shows,but always as a spectator.<BR>So how does it work?<BR>Do you need to be a member of these "clubs"?<BR>Average cost ?<BR>Do all shows judge car,or just some?<BR>If I left a question out, I should of asked<BR>please feel free to volunteer the info.<P>Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||stimpy||03-17-2001||08:43 AM||||Duhhh, I guess I coulda looked at a calander myself, but I coulda <B>sworn</B>...<P>Anyhow, Tina, I can only speak on FCO's policies re the show.  All entrants are welcome. Our entry fee is around $20 and includes t-shirt, various goodies. Cars are judged in their respective classes, but it's mostly just about fun. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Sevaan||03-17-2001||08:58 AM||||No Canadian shows?||||reg||1
Z||000012||Old Lar||03-17-2001||09:47 AM||||GTA (Greater Toronto Area) usually has a show.  I went last year (September I think). Lots of people from Michigan came.  An international flair.  There were lots of non participant Fieros in the the parking lot.  Everyone goes to the shows for their own personal reasons, I go for the fun.||||reg||3
Z||000013||Oreif||03-17-2001||11:02 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tina:<BR><B>O.K, rather than calling some of these<BR>people and asking all the dumb Questions.<BR>Perhaps, you guys and girls can fill in the blanks.<BR> <BR>Been to car shows,but always as a spectator.<BR>So how does it work?<BR>Do you need to be a member of these "clubs"?<BR>Average cost ?<BR>Do all shows judge car,or just some?<BR>If I left a question out, I should of asked<BR>please feel free to volunteer the info.<P>Thanks</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Tine, I have been to a few shows. There is a cost. Usually the fee is $10 to $25. Most entries get a "goodie bag" It's filled with items from the sponsors. All cars are judged (at the shows I go to) The cars are usually divided into classes. If it is NOT a Fiero show, You can get put into the same group as a custom Fiero. It usually depends on the amount of Fieros at a show. If only a few show up they are usually grouped together. As for club shows, they generally break them up by years and custom cars are usually in their own group. Our NIFE Fierorama, Is for "Daily Driver" cars. The custom cars are usually in the "Display Class" and are not judged. Cars are broken into groups by years and mileage. The fee is $10.00 unless you are a member than it's free (Yearly subscription to the club is $20)<BR>As for voting, some shows have a panel of judges others give the entrants a form to fill out. So the judging is done by all who enter. (NIFE does it this way)<BR>Prizes are usually trophies or certificates. Usually the higher fee ones have larger trophies. If you go to a car show expecting to win you will be dis-appointed often. If you go just to show off your car and see other cars, when you win occasionally it feels great. The main thing is to have a good time.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 03-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||Tina||03-17-2001||11:42 AM||||Thanks.<BR>Although I'am one of the few women who gets upset when I get a stain on my intake.<BR>I won't go as far as carrying armor-all in the purse.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>This is my daily driver(grocery-getter)in the summer.<BR>No, not in for the trophy's.<BR>Just for good times, and perhaps meet some other Fieroholics.<P>||||reg||1
